A||||12||Nashco||Where to get exhaust system in Alabama?||||1||
Z||000000||Nashco||05-24-2001||01:29 AM||||Hey everybody, here's my obligatory post of the week <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I just got a 80 series Flowmaster for my fiero, and I need to get a new cat and pipe from the y-pipe installed.  My old exhaust it COMPLETELY shot, and I need to get new everything from the y-pipe back installed very soon.<P>Has anybody in 'bama dealt with a good shop getting exhaust done?  I'm not from around here (I'm in the Anniston area), and I really need to get this done ASAP.  I was hoping there would be somewhere local, or somewhere I could take it on a Saturday.  If it's local I can drop it off, if not I'd hang out all day on a Saturday.<P>Price is a factor, but I'm looking for a good job.  I want to use all aluminized pipe so I don't have to worry about rusting (quick rusting anyway...hard to avoid without stainless).  I have the ability to do just about anything to my car, but it will be easier to take it to a shop and get pipe bent than to try and make it from mandrel bends over a weekend.<P>Lastly, what have you done with your exhaust hangers?  I've noticed the spring suspended hangers; how have you gone about installing new hangers?  I could re-use them, I understand, but I'm sure a shop wouldn't be too keen on grinding and re-welding the tabs.  Are they easier to make the tabs?<P>I really appreciate your help everybody!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jefrysuko||05-24-2001||02:11 AM||||There is one and only one place you should take your Fiero in Alabama!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#top" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#top</A> <P>------------------<BR>Jeffrey D Suckow<BR>88 GT<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:Jefrysuko@aol.com">Jefrysuko@aol.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||05-24-2001||02:20 AM||||I know that would be ideal...but I want fresh pipes, not used.  Also, this is all bigger pipe anyway (2.5" inlets and outlets on the muffler).  I also need a new 2.5" converter.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jefrysuko||05-24-2001||02:25 AM||||Ed does custom work dosn't he?  At the very least you had ought to call him and see if he recomends someone.  He sure is a nice enough guy to talk to.<P>------------------<BR>Jeffrey D Suckow<BR>88 GT<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:Jefrysuko@aol.com">Jefrysuko@aol.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||05-24-2001||02:42 AM||||I'll definitely call and ask for a recommendation, I was planning on calling anyhow.  I was there for the swap meet last month, and didn't notice a pipe bender anywhere, so I assumed he didn't...?  They did have a lot of parts though! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||05-24-2001||02:22 PM||||Email me- I think that I can help.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cooter||05-24-2001||06:44 PM||||Oops- don't email me. My AOL account is screwed up and I can only get the Forum at work. Go to Faulkner Brothers Grocery on Choccolocco Road near Hiway 9. Ask for Steve and tell him what you are trying to do. He did the duals on my Fiero and it looks/sounds great!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Nashco||05-25-2001||02:15 AM||||Alright Cooter, I'll figure out where that's at tomorrow night probably.  Does he work days or nights?  If I just walk up and ask somebody, will they know who he is or should I have a last name?  I'm assuming it'll be easy to find him, but I wouldn't want to make a trip there only to look like a bumbling idiot <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>What do you mean he did your duals?  You have a true dual exhuast?  Any pics?  I considered it for the longest time, but figured I'd run with the tried system, as I can't afford to have any problems with my daily driver right now.<P>Thanks<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||Nashco||05-30-2001||01:24 AM||||Cooter, you there?  I would just cruise up to the place, but I have to make a special time to do it and leave work.<P>I work 55-60 hours a week (trying to support myself sucks <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">) and I'm gone pretty much every day from 6:30 am to 7 pm.  If I need to talk to this guy in person, I'll have to make a trip during lunch or work early or something.<P>Do you have another way I can get a hold of him, or any more details on when I should meet him?  I'm getting kind of antsy because I need this done within about three weeks, before I move out of state again.<P>Thanks, I really appreciate all your help with things <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000009||Nashco||10-15-2001||02:41 AM||||Cooter, I hope you take a look at this.  I am back down here in 'bama and I <u>need</u> to get my exhaust done.  It's now been about a thousand miles since last time I said that, and, obviously way too long <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I am ready to get this done, and would love to do it locally if you know who can take care of me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I am considering leaving work early Tuesday and finding Steve at this Grocery, in hopes he's still there.  I've had somebody recommend the local Midas *snicker*, which I will check out then too.  Lastly, there is a place in Trussville that has been recommended that uses a mandrel bender and does quality work for a fair price.  The mandrel bending would be a bonus, but not required.  Hopefully you get this, and can help me out.  Thanks, and if you'd rather do this over PM or email, you know how! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||Nashco||10-15-2001||10:26 PM||||bump...last time||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cooter||10-15-2001||11:28 PM||||As far as I know, Steve is still working at the store. Call them as soon as you can and make sure because I'd hate to see you drive out there for nothing. I don't have a phone book handy to get the number, but it is listed as Faulkner Brothers' Grocery on highway 9 in Choccolocco (I think that is spelled right) Shoot me an email if you need help finding the place.<P>Greg||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula88||10-16-2001||12:34 AM||||My recommendation is to check out West Coast Fiero.  They have a complete 2.5" exhaust from the Y-pipe out available, plus hi flo cats and mufflers (I know you've already got your Flowie).  Their website <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com</A>  says the Fiero exhaust system is in development, but Chris told me in an email that special orders are being shipped.  That's my plan for my Formula this winter.  Complete new 2.5" exhaust with a high-flow cat and a SpinTech muffler.<p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 10-16-2001).]||||reg||14
